                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Super Lovely Planet, the newest installment in the Lovely Planet series. \n\nChanging up the genre of the previous games from First Person Shooter/Platformer to a Third Person Platformer is a very risky step and you have to give the dev some credit for trying out something new. But does it work out in the end and is Super Lovely Planet as good as its predecessors? \n\nIn its core the game is still a high precision platformer focused on speedrunning with the same lovely aesthetics and the same level of challenge. The new control scheme may take some time getting used to but after a while it feels as tight as always. If you played the previous games you are probably familiar with the charm of the game, the dev knows how to craft a game world and they did it again this time. The atmosphere is just as good as in the original Lovely Planet and everything is filled with secrets to explore and stories to discover. There is a variety of enemies and obstacles that you encounter throughout various differently themed worlds while making your way through this new adventure to provide a gripping experience for new players and veterans. Oh and did I mention that the soundtrack is great? \n\nSo in the end does this change to the series work out and bring in some fresh air? If you ask me it totally does. Super Lovely Planet is a great addition to the series and I can recommend it to all the fans of the original game or people that enjoy high precision platforming in general.",
